He had let her get to the end without telling her that he had been the one who argued for the array.
 He had come close twice there too.
 Both times the sentence had assembled itself —
 *I fought for that and I lost* —
 and both times he had heard what it would sound like coming down a telephone line to a woman he had not spoken to in twenty years,
 and had put it away.
 It was not a thing you said in order to be useful.
 It was a thing you said in order to be forgiven,
 and she had not accused him of anything,
 and a man who apologises for a charge nobody has laid is telling you what he thinks he did.
\end_layout

